* BAS416 low-leakage switching diode (Nexperia), fitted here: Nexperia supplies no
* SPICE model on the product page.
* IS and N are fitted to two maximum forward-voltage points of the datasheet
* (Table 7, Tj = 25 C): VF = 0.9 V at 1 mA and 1.0 V at 10 mA.
*   N  = (1.0 - 0.9) / (Vt ln 10) = 0.1 / (0.02585 * 2.3026) = 1.68
*   IS = 1e-3 / exp(0.9 / (N Vt))  = 1.0e-12 A
* So VF at 0.5 mA is 0.87 V (worst case); the datasheet's typical curve sits lower.
* Not modelled: series resistance (VF above ~10 mA), capacitance, recovery, and the
* datasheet's reverse leakage (max 5 nA at 75 V, 25 C; ~13 nA at 70 C, Fig. 4). The
* reverse current here is IS (1 pA) plus ngspice's GMIN.
.model BAS416 D(IS=1e-12 N=1.68)
